diff --git a/docs/business-rules.md b/docs/business-rules.md
index 7a3126a..90f7688 100644
--- a/docs/business-rules.md
+++ b/docs/business-rules.md
@@ -126,13 +126,29 @@ ## Subscription and Access
 - Asaas webhooks update subscription state idempotently (implementation: see Asaas skill when available in repo).
 - Transactional emails (invitation, password reset, billing notices) via **Resend**.
 
+## Authentication
+
+Session-based login for staff accounts (`users`), written in the app (no starter kit): Livewire full-page `login` / `register` and plain controllers for logout, password reset and e-mail verification.
+
+| Rule | Detail |
+| ---- | ------ |
+| Guests only | `login`, `register` and the password-reset routes redirect authenticated users to `home`. |
+| Login throttling | 5 failed attempts per lowercase e-mail + IP, then an `auth.throttle` error on `email`; a successful login clears the counter and regenerates the session. |
+| Registration throttling | 5 attempts per IP (every attempt counts, valid or not, so the "unique e-mail" error is not a free oracle). Accounts start unverified and the `Registered` event sends the verification mail. |
+| Password policy | One rule for every new password (`Password::defaults()`): min 8, letters, mixed case, numbers. |
+| Home access | `/home` needs `auth` + `verified`: guests go to `login`, unverified users to `verification.notice`. |
+| Forgot password | Always answers with the same `status` (never reveals whether the e-mail exists); 6 requests/minute. |
+| Reset password | Validates token, e-mail and the password policy; rotates `remember_token` and fires `PasswordReset`. An unknown e-mail looks like an invalid token. |
+| E-mail verification | Signed + throttled link that only verifies the logged-in user (tampered id/hash → 403). Resending to a verified user sends nothing. |
+| Logout | POST only; invalidates the session and regenerates the CSRF token. |
+
 ## Observability
 
 Relevant operational events (webhook failures, queue errors, plan limits) can be forwarded by **webhooks** to a dedicated **Discord** server — only alerts, does not replace application logs.
 
 ## Multilingual
 
-Web interface and **totem API** responses must support multiple languages; business rules (priorities, queue labels) are configurable per entity with locale fallback.
+Web interface and **totem API** responses must support multiple languages. The web app defaults to **Brazilian Portuguese** (`APP_LOCALE=pt_BR`) with **English** as fallback; screen text lives in `lang/{en,pt_BR}/ui.php`, never in views; business rules (priorities, queue labels) are configurable per entity with locale fallback.
 
